Step 1: Input Graph
 Read the number of vertices V.
 Read the number of edges E.
 Enter the source, destination and weight of every edge.
Step 2: Update Edge Weight
 Enter the source and destination of the edge whose weight has to be updated.
 Enter the new weight.
 Search for the corresponding edge and update its weight.
Step 3: Apply Kruskal’s Algorithm
 Sort all edges in ascending order of weight.
 Initialize every vertex as a separate set.
 Select the smallest remaining edge.
 Check whether adding the edge creates a cycle.
 If it does not create a cycle:
 Add the edge to the MST.
 Add its weight to the total cost.
 Display the selected edge and running total.
 If it creates a cycle, reject the edge.
 Continue until V - 1 edges are selected or all edges are processed.
Step 4: Check Connectivity
 If the number of selected edges is V - 1, the MST is successfully formed.
 Otherwise, the graph is disconnected and an MST cannot be formed.
 Display the result and total cost.
 Stop.
